esis. '\n'Provisional mechanism: retaining P(M_t), add a zero-start head-specific map Q_t(M_t - mean_s M_s) to preserve relative task rank content at the final readout without feeding it back into shared tokens. An active common-source control Q_t(mean_s M_s) tests whether added task-specific matrix capacity alone suffices. '\n'Lineage review constrains this choice: R13 contextual scoring (memory-private 0.8309696093096159; static-private 0.8309294998382515; mean counterparts 0.8303638539316801/0.8304330439477664) did not beat R12; R14 input-gradient blocking (click 0.8308403372592208, auxiliary 0.8305847950391266, both 0.8305824963765673) did not beat open 0.8310755947860231. R14-open repeats the identical seed/result and is a replay, not independent replication. '\n'R15 private trunks64 0.8309133862899759 and shared trunk210 0.8309514201872332 added about 77k parameters without beating R12. R16 private summary exchange 0.8300677128487329 and mean exchange 0.830158082387002 both lost to R12 and g0; the private-minus-mean effect is -0.0000903695382691. This opposes that early-exchange implementation, not all task conditioning. No failed execution appears among the 19 supplied trajectories; scientifically unsuccessful successful executions are retained as negative evidence. Historical candidate_diagnostics are not_requested, not proof of passed numeric gates. '\n'This is a local extension of inherited components, with no priority claim or established gradient-interference mechanism.'),\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'trial://g3-r0012-memory_task_private_linear','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'candidate.py initially matched its committed SHA256 32b0c84cf45766aba1ea0196e550baaa63faf798c86863477f4f9484ef36730f exactly. Preserve its private content and shared rank projection and append four task-specific contrast/common maps after all inherited initialization.'},\n {'source_ref':'trial://g0-r0011-memory_joint_collapsed','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Retain g0 joint/collapsed feedback memory, relation/time summary tokens, forward masks, unnormalized DIN event pooling and four towers through R12; the added maps act only at final task readout.'},\n {'source_ref':'trial://g3-r0010-content_plus_linear_private','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inherit its task-specific signed content/rank readout through R12, while retaining the g0 representation and appending an across-task contrast of existing rank summaries.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived exact-version primary text lines251-283 inspected: target-conditioned unnormalized weighted history sum is inherited. The four-task rank-contrast maps and memory tokens are local adaptations, not DIN reproduction or evidence of novelty.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned primary benchmark code lines123-169 and258-313 inspected: task-masked sequence hubs, task-token readouts and affine broadcast are adjacent task-specific information flow. Here no hubs, new attention or broadcast are added: a single linear contrast of four learned rank summaries reaches existing towers. This is a benchmark-code comparison, not equivalence to the original paper.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:infnet','verification':'discovered','difference':'Resolved original-paper provenance and attempted authorized read; detailed original text is unavailable. Inspected labeled UniRank section2.3 fallback and pinned benchmark code. Exact original-method overlap and priority remain unverified.'}\n],\n'inherited_components':[\n'Entire R12 source at SHA256 32b0c84cf45766aba1ea0196e550baaa63faf798c86863477f4f9484ef36730f except declared architecture-config/constructor additions, one added rank residual call and helper; no inherited functions replaced.',\n'g0 six item-field embeddings plus historical action values; static fields; five rank windows and seven target-relation summaries; full linear moments, relation/content banks, factorized feedback-content path, joint/collapsed feedback memory and JointBlock.',\n'R12 shared relevance trunk64, four private scorers, open scorer-input gradients, unnormalized signed content summaries, shared linear-rank projection P, global DIN residual and four prediction towers.',\n'Existing masked-ID sanitization before embedding/Dice and current-action zeroing, causal feature boundary, module initialization/RNG order; host optimizers, precision, labels, splits, sum-BCE loss and scoring unchanged.'\n],\n'proposed_difference':(\n'For existing FP32 extra summaries M in [B,4,112], compute mean Mbar over the task axis and D_t=M_t-Mbar in every arm. Append task_rank_bank with shape [4,112,112], initialized to zero after all inherited initialization; no bias or random draws. Each task readout remains C_t+P(M_t), augmented by D_t @ Q_t in candidate task_rank_contrast, or Mbar @ Q_t in control task_rank_common. The original shared DIN sum is still added in forward. Both sources are materialized contiguous and the same FP32 einsum btv,tvw->btw is executed. All source values derive only from the existing visible histories and relevance scorers. The task mean uses all four prediction-task summaries, not current labels. No new training-loss hook, attention, shared-memory update, external input or data pass is introduced. '\n'Both arms keep task_routing private; the control changes only the source of the new maps, never the inherited M_t or C_t. Zero banks are an initialization replay, not an inactive experimental arm. The common control can learn distinct Q_t and remains active whenever Mbar is nonzero. Expected new parameters per arm 4*112*112=50176, total33119433, embedding31793216, dense1326217; host counts authoritative.'),\n'predictions':[\n'Primary directional prediction: task_rank_contrast exceeds both R12 macro AUC 0.8310755947860231 and task_rank_common at the same seed and full frozen protocol. Exceeding only g0/g3 source bests is insufficient for incremental mechanism support. Select on validation four-task macro AUC with declared Logloss/parameters/trial-ID ties; never use click alone or introduce a per-task veto.',\n'If task-specific rank deviations add information, the contrast arm will improve the relative rare-task readout compared with common source; report all four AUC/Logloss deltas even if the macro gain masks a regression. Buy gains are a predeclared diagnostic direction, not a selection rule.',\n'At paired construction, all inherited parameters/buffers and CPU RNG states should match R12. With zero Q both arms should replay R12 initial predictions, inherited gradients and Dice-buffer updates. At initialization all scorer outputs and M are zero, so Q gradients are expected zero until scorers open.',\n'With diagnostic nonzero Q and nondegenerate M: isolated contrast update is invariant to adding one common vector to every M_t, while isolated common update changes; isolated common update is invariant to zero-task-mean perturbations, while the contrast update can change. Apply these tests to the helper only because inherited P(M_t) changes in both full models. Empty-history rank residual is exactly zero for any finite Q.',\n'Parameter counts and nominal forward operators are equal across the new arms. Additional contraction is 4*112*112 MACs/example (411041792 at batch8192); report measured training/full wall and inference latency/throughput/peak GPU memory rather than infer equal compute from parameter equality.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n'Failure to beat R12, or a tie/loss to the active common-source control, opposes incremental task-contrast utility for this implementation. If both additions win equally, evidence favors added maps/optimization capacity rather than task-contrast information. A control win opposes the directional hypothesis and remains eligible under the same selection rule.',\n'Loss of an apparent improvement under a genuinely different paired seed weakens repeated support; an identical-seed replay is not independent evidence. No significance claim from these single-seed validation comparisons.',\n'Any changed inherited initialization, label-dependent forward path, invalid output shape/nonfinite gradients, masked-ID/current-action dependence, inactive common control on a nondegenerate diagnostic, or nonzero empty-history residual invalidates the implementation before scientific scoring.',\n'If measured cost makes the selected arm dominated by R12 on quality and compute, no efficiency benefit is established even with a small quality gain. The common/contrast source contrast alone cannot establish shared-gradient conflict.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n'Added functional capacity or redundant parameterization with shared P, rather than unique rank evidence; active common-source replacement and historical R15 capacity failures reduce but do not eliminate this explanation.',\n'Contrast and mean differ in signal variance, correlation, gradient coupling and BF16 rounding. They are equal-parameter/operator replacements, not identical functional families or equal effective backward cost. No variance-normalized control is claimed within this budget.',\n'The existing nonlinear towers can already apply task-specific transforms. A null result may mean the extra linear maps are redundant or learn too slowly because rank summaries and zero-start output projections open late during the single pass; it does not refute all task-specific temporal representations.',\n'Validation adaptation across many trials, rare-task label counts and seed-dependent optimization can explain small gains. Three paired seeds and unseen-data confirmation are not guaranteed; held-out data are unavailable and must never enter this phase.',\n'Inherited official_offline histories and static snapshots have unestablished production point-in-time validity; cart/fav/buy labels concern user/category/brand within24h rather than advertisement-attributed conversion. Relative rank is not elapsed time.',\n'Raw parquet files/digests, sample predictions and user grouping are not exposed here. The pinned host protocol and receipts are the reproducibility boundary; do not invent a local dataset audit, user bootstrap or new slices.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n {'parent_ref':parent,'intervention':'task_rank_contrast: C_t+P(M_t)+(M_t-Mbar)@Q_t in each final readout.','control':'task_rank_common: C_t+P(M_t)+Mbar@Q_t; identical new matrices/zero initialization and FP32 contraction. Both retain the incumbent private content/rank path.',\n  'held_fixed':['Full protocol hash '+protocol,'Data identity9f110bfc2f037f36e2f48787b812df640fe5df2de1cda8db7ac04590c1c9be44 and released split/visibility','Seed20262027, one epoch, batch8192,100-history limit, BF16/TF32-off, host optimizers and sum-four-BCE','Every inherited parameter initialization, Dice buffer, CPU RNG stream, task scoring and shared P','New map shapes, initialization, source construction, contiguous layout and FP32 contraction'],\n  'remaining_confounds':['Mean versus contrast signal scale and cross-task gradients','One-seed full-validation adaptation; repeated support pending','Different effective backward paths may change measured runtime'],\n  'decision_if_supported':'Only if contrast beats common and R12, retain it as provisional task-contrast support, freeze exact source/config and comparison suite, then use the reserved validation repetition if admissible. Report source-best and all-task/cost deltas.',\n  'decision_if_not_supported':'Keep negative/failed receipts. If both additions fail, retain R12 and redirect assessment reserve to a paired R12-versus-g0 validation repetition. If common wins, select it only by the fixed rule and label task-contrast hypothesis unsupported; do not rename its gain as contrast support.'},\n {'parent_ref':parent,'intervention':'Compare both complete new arms with frozen R12 and source bests g0-r0011-memory_joint_collapsed and g3-r0010-content_plus_linear_private.','control':'Existing same-data/seed/recipe R12, plus DIN initial reference; R12 private/mean by linear/copy factorial and R13/R14/R15/R16 branches provide lineage constraints, not independent repetitions.',\n  'held_fixed':['Same validation sample count2871767 and four-task scoring','Same training information and host recipe','Source configs/hashes from committed receipts'],\n  'remaining_confounds':['Extra50176 dense parameters and added contraction versus R12','Historical controls include only one independent seed','R13/R15/R16 are distinct interventions, not clean controls for the new bank'],\n  'decision_if_supported':'Require measured benefit relative to R12 and the equal-parameter common control before attributing the new source, then separate architectural utility from cost-frontier claims.',\n  'decision_if_not_supported':'Retain R12 as the best measured incumbent, report null or negative task-rank evidence and the unresolved next question: does rank projection learn fast enough after zero scorers open? No further rank-variant tuning is reserved.'}\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n'estimate_ref':('Runtime context remaining_seconds snapshot3065.6248013973236; protocol deadline_unix1794241824.5008233 and trial_cap_seconds1208.5413760878146 remain hard limits. Empirical full-unit costs: R12 594.1056s (train541.7392, inference43.0601), g0 493.4548s, R16 603.6-604.7s, R15 wider arms651.0-682.3s. Budget new arms at650s each as an estimate, not a cap override or guaranteed runtime; one new bank has50176 parameters and411041792 MACs/batch8192. Initial-clock audit gave2861.9835s remaining; preparation continues to consume it. Host numerical gates and actual costs determine admissibility.'),\n'all_variants_counted':True,\n'attribution_reserve':'One candidate plus one active equal-parameter source replacement, count both full runs (~1300s). Reserve up to100s for necessary host numerical/masking/gradient/initialization diagnostics across the two sources, not uncharged calibration. All repeated attempts, diagnostics, failures and unfinished jobs are charged. No automated retry after unknown execution state. Existing R12/g0/g3 and all negative trajectories remain frozen; no third exploratory variant.',\n'assessment_reserve':'Reserve1200s after source checks and planned two-arm study, with no test scoring. Before each job host must recompute deadline slack using measured costs and avoid consuming this reserve for screening. Freeze the validation comparison suite and exact sources/configs before any assessment repetition. If a new arm is selected and fits, repeat selected arm and closest new-arm control at one new common seed (two runs,~1200s); R12/g0 comparisons then remain seed1-only. If neither arm improves R12, repeat R12 and g0 at one new common seed (~1090s). Seed choice is host-owned and prospectively fixed; do not override frozen host seed in CONFIG. Full three-seed paired assessment of candidate/control/R12/g0 cannot fit this remaining budget; report the missing repetitions and any omitted two-seed assessment plainly. This proposal does not authorize training in the coding jail.',\n'stop_rule':'Never extend the deadline or trial cap. Before the first training arm, require fresh remaining time sufficient for both estimated650s arms,100s gates and1200s assessment plus host overhead; otherwise skip the new two-arm study and retain R12 for admissible validation assessment. Once measured cost or a failed gate prevents the remaining controlled comparison and reserve fitting, stop new exploration, preserve all receipts, and assess only an already frozen supported comparison if it fits. If no useful complete experiment fits, stop with preliminary existing evidence; budget exhaustion is not scientific success.'\n}}\nchecks=(\n'Host reproduction: import the listed standalone module, instantiate Model(feature_map, **CONFIG), and execute the existing host trainer under protocol '+protocol+'. No host CLI or data files 